i2pd (2.61.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Debian package now ships the complete documentation tree, branding,
    ChangeLog, LICENSE, NOTICE, the tools licence and the i2pd/i2pdctl man
    pages from the CMake install. The TUI package owns its own man page.
  * An existing /var/lib/i2pd/certificates directory is moved to
    /var/lib/i2pd/certificates.dpkg-old before the packaged compatibility
    symlink is installed. Move any locally added trust anchors back into
    /var/lib/i2pd/certificates after the upgrade, or configure certsdir.
  * The AppArmor profile is now loaded and reloaded by dh_apparmor and permits
    the optional privilege-separation workers to re-exec the router binary.
    TUI and I2PControl sockets under /run/i2pd are allowed.
  * The TUI package now declares Breaks/Replaces for the old i2pd binary
    package, so upgrading from 2.61.0-2 or earlier does not fail on the moved
    /usr/bin/i2pd-tui file.

 -- openi2pd maintainers <daviduhden@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

i2pd (2.61.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The desktop entry now belongs to i2pd-tui and launches i2pd-tui instead
    of starting a second router. The packaged service remains the only
    router process.
  * Existing /var/lib/i2pd, /var/log/i2pd and /run/i2pd ownership and modes
    are no longer reset on upgrade. New installations use 0700 for the
    private state, log and runtime directories.
  * The package now ships the i2pd-tools licence notice and a CC-BY-SA-4.0
    notice for the first-party documentation that declares that license.

 -- openi2pd maintainers <daviduhden@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

i2pd (2.61.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The SysV fallback starts the foreground router in the background as the
    dedicated i2pd user. The systemd unit uses systemd's native
    StateDirectory=/RuntimeDirectory= for /var/lib/i2pd and /run/i2pd; the
    tmpfiles policy creates those paths plus /var/log/i2pd when
    systemd-tmpfiles is used.
  * If you copied an older i2pd.service or started i2pd from a custom
    foreground unit, review or remove that copy before upgrading. Two units
    can start two routers against the same /var/lib/i2pd and corrupt it.
  * The ncurses TUI is now in the separate i2pd-tui package. Install it if
    you use i2pd-tui; the i2pd package no longer ships that binary.
  * Configuration stays in /etc/i2pd. The old /var/lib/i2pd configuration and
    tunnel symlinks are no longer created; only the certificate compatibility
    link is retained.

 -- openi2pd maintainers <daviduhden@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
